<title>USA: Telephone problems delayed NU earnings.</title>
<headline>Telephone problems delayed NU earnings.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Problems with Southern New England Telecommunications Corp's &quot;blast fax&quot; service delayed Northeast Utilities' report of its fourth quarter and full year results more than an hour, spokesman Jeffrey R. Kotkin said.</p>
<p>The results were eventually released and Northeast reported a fourth quarter share loss of $0.60 vs a profit of $0.50 in the year-ago period.</p>
<p>Kotkin said at 1710 EST/2310 GMT that the release had been running about an hour late.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.))</p>
